.TH VERBISAGED 1 "September 2026" "Verbisage 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
verbisaged \- serve dictionary completion and spelling requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B verbisaged
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verbisaged serves dictionary operations over the session D-Bus or a
line-oriented JSON protocol on standard input and output. The packaged
session service starts it on demand with --mode dbus. It does not require
a system-bus service or administrator privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --mode " mode"
Select dbus or stdio server operation.
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read an explicit configuration file.
.TP
.BI --language " tag"
Set the default language, such as en_US.
.TP
.BI --backend " chain"
Override the configured backend chain.
.TP
.B --verbose
Write diagnostic details to standard error.
.TP
.B --help
Display all supported dictionary and configuration options.
.SH D-BUS INTERFACE
The session name is org.verbisage.Dictionary, object path
/org/verbisage/Dictionary and interface org.verbisage.Dictionary1.
.PP
Complete(word, max, language) returns ranked word/score pairs combining
current-word prefixes and single-edit corrections. It omits the exact input,
which callers should preserve as a separate literal choice. Scores are
relative heuristics, not probabilities. The maximum response is 100 entries;
input is limited to 128 Unicode characters and 512 UTF-8 bytes.
.PP
QueryLimited, Query, Suggest, IsCorrect, Frequency and Predict remain
available. AddWord and BumpNgram report unsupported operations for the
read-only packaged Patricia data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/verbisage/config.toml
Default system configuration.
.TP
.B ~/.config/verbisage/config.toml
An existing user configuration overrides the system file. An absolute
XDG_CONFIG_HOME replaces ~/.config. An explicit --config overrides both.
.TP
.B /usr/share/android-patricia-dictionaries/en_US.dict
English dictionary supplied by the separate language-data package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR verbisage (1)
